Every failure mode a References header can have, in one header:

  * an unterminated angle-addr (the first entry has no closing '>'),
  * an empty '<>' entry,
  * a bare token that is not an angle-addr,
  * a duplicate of an earlier entry,
  * a reference to a message that does not exist in the store,
  * and an In-Reply-To that matches nothing at all.

The threading pass must still place this message somewhere sensible
rather than panicking or dropping it.
